{"id":"mahabharata-12-260","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":260,"title":"षष्ट्यधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 260 · Syumarashmi asks Kapila about action","summary":{"en":"Yudhishthira asks about the dharma that joins the giving up of beings with the six qualities of policy, and Bhishma tells of the sage Kapila and the brahmin Syumarashmi. They debate whether the sacrifice with violence is dharma, and Kapila speaks of the four paths of the gods.","kn":"ಜೀವಿಗಳ ತ್ಯಾಗ ಮತ್ತು ಷಾಡ್ಗುಣ್ಯ ಸೇರಿಸುವ ಧರ್ಮದ ಬಗ್ಗೆ ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಋಷಿ ಕಪಿಲ ಮತ್ತು ಬ್ರಾಹ್ಮಣ ಸ್ಯೂಮರಶ್ಮಿಯ ಕಥೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಹಿಂಸೆಯ ಯಜ್ಞ ಧರ್ಮವೇ ಎಂದು ಅವರು ವಾದಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ, ಕಪಿಲ ದೇವಯಾನದ ನಾಲ್ಕು ಮಾರ್ಗಗಳನ್ನು ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"युधिष्ठिर प्राणियों के विरोध-रहित त्याग और छह गुणों का मेल करने वाले धर्म के बारे में पूछते हैं, और भीष्म ऋषि कपिल और ब्राह्मण स्यूमरश्मि की कथा सुनाते हैं। वे बहस करते हैं कि हिंसा वाला यज्ञ धर्म है या नहीं, और कपिल देवयान के चार मार्ग बताते हैं।","te":"జీవులకు విరోధం లేని త్యాగం, షాడ్గుణ్యాలను కలిపే ధర్మం గురించి యుధిష్ఠిరుడు అడుగుతాడు; భీష్ముడు ఋషి కపిలుడు, బ్రాహ్మణుడు స్యూమరశ్మి కథ చెబుతాడు. హింసతో కూడిన యజ్ఞం ధర్మమా అని వాదిస్తారు, కపిలుడు దేవయానం నాలుగు మార్గాలను చెబుతాడు.","ta":"உயிர்களுக்கு முரணற்ற துறவும் ஆறு குணங்களும் இணைக்கும் தர்மம் பற்றி யுதிஷ்டிரர் கேட்க, முனிவர் கபிலர், அந்தணர் ஸ்யூமரஷ்மி கதையைப் பீஷ்மர் கூறுகிறார். வன்முறை வேள்வி தர்மமா என்று வாதிடுகின்றனர், கபிலர் தேவயானத்தின் நான்கு வழிகளைக் கூறுகிறார்.","ml":"ജീവികളെ ത്യജിക്കുന്നതിനോടും ആറു നയഗുണങ്ങളോടും ചേരുന്ന ധർമ്മമേതെന്ന് യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ ചോദിക്കുന്നു; കപിലനും ശ്യുമരശ്മി എന്ന ബ്രാഹ്മണനും തമ്മിലുള്ള കഥ ഭീഷ്മർ പറയുന്നു. ഹിംസയോടെയുള്ള യജ്ഞം ധർമ്മമാണോ എന്ന് അവർ തർക്കിക്കുന്നു; ദേവന്മാരുടെ നാലു വഴികളെക്കുറിച്ച് കപിലൻ സംസാരിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.260; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"मोक्षधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Mokshadharma Parva (Duties for liberation)","verses":[{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"अविरोधेन भूतानां त्यागः षाड्गुण्यकारकः ।\nयः स्यादुभयभाग्धर्मस्तन्मे ब्रूहि पितामह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Grandfather, tell me the dharma that is renunciation without harming beings, which yields the sixfold policy and brings a share in both worlds."}},{"n":2,"text":"गार्हस्थ्यस्य च धर्मस्य त्यागधर्मस्य चोभयोः ।\nअदूरसंप्रस्थितयोः किं स्विच्छ्रेयः पितामह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Of the householder's dharma and the dharma of renunciation, both set out not far apart, which is better, grandfather?"}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":3,"text":"उभौ धर्मौ महाभागावुभौ परमदुश्चरौ ।\nउभौ महाफलौ तात सद्भिराचरितावुभौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Both dharmas are great, both are exceedingly hard to practice, both bear great fruit, dear son, and both are followed by the good."}},{"n":4,"text":"अत्र ते वर्तयिष्यामि प्रामाण्यमुभयोस्तयोः ।\nशृणुष्वैकमनाः पार्थ छिन्नधर्मार्थसंशयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"On this I shall tell you the authority of each. Listen with one mind, Partha, and your doubt over dharma and its aim will be cut."}},{"n":5,"text":"अत्राप्युदाहरन्तीममितिहासं पुरातनम् ।\nकपिलस्य गोश्च संवादं तन्निबोध युधिष्ठिर ॥","meaning":{"en":"On this too they tell this ancient tale, a conversation of Kapila and a cow. Understand it, Yudhishthira."}},{"n":6,"text":"आम्नायमनुपश्यन्हि पुराणं शाश्वतं ध्रुवम् ।\nनहुषः पूर्वमालेभे त्वष्टुर्गामिति नः श्रुतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Looking to the ancient, eternal, fixed tradition: we have heard that Nahusha once seized Tvashtri's cow for sacrifice."}},{"n":7,"text":"तां नियुक्तामदीनात्मा सत्त्वस्थः समये रतः ।\nज्ञानवान्नियताहारो ददर्श कपिलस्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kapila, undismayed, steady in goodness, devoted to his vow, learned and temperate in food, then saw her bound for sacrifice."}},{"n":8,"text":"स बुद्धिमुत्तमां प्राप्तो नैष्ठिकीमकुतोभयाम् ।\nस्मरामि शिथिलं सत्यं वेदा इत्यब्रवीत्सकृत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He had reached the highest settled understanding, free of all fear, and once said, \"I remember truth, but it seems loose; so say the Vedas.\""}},{"n":9,"text":"तां गामृषिः स्यूमरश्मिः प्रविश्य यतिमब्रवीत् ।\nहंहो वेदा यदि मता धर्माः केनापरे मताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sage Syumarashmi entered that cow and spoke to the ascetic: \"Ho! If the Vedas are authoritative, by what are other dharmas held authoritative?"}},{"n":10,"text":"तपस्विनो धृतिमतः श्रुतिविज्ञानचक्षुषः ।\nसर्वमार्षं हि मन्यन्ते व्याहृतं विदितात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ascetics, steadfast, with the eye of scriptural knowledge, regard everything spoken by the sages as authoritative, they who know the self."}},{"n":11,"text":"तस्यैवं गततृष्णस्य विज्वरस्य निराशिषः ।\nका विवक्षास्ति वेदेषु निरारम्भस्य सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For him who is free of craving, free of fever, without wishes and undertakings of every kind, what purpose is there in the Vedas?\""}},{"text":"कपिल उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Kapila said:"}},{"n":12,"text":"नाहं वेदान्विनिन्दामि न विवक्षामि कर्हिचित् ।\nपृथगाश्रमिणां कर्माण्येकार्थानीति नः श्रुतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I do not condemn the Vedas, nor do I ever wish to. We have heard that the duties of those in different stages of life have one aim."}},{"n":13,"text":"गच्छत्येव परित्यागी वानप्रस्थश्च गच्छति ।\nगृहस्थो ब्रह्मचारी च उभौ तावपि गच्छतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The renouncer goes, the forest-dweller goes, and the householder and student both go as well."}},{"n":14,"text":"देवयाना हि पन्थानश्चत्वारः शाश्वता मताः ।\nतेषां ज्यायःकनीयस्त्वं फलेषूक्तं बलाबलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The four paths of the gods are held to be eternal; among them greater and lesser are spoken of in the strength and weakness of their fruits."}},{"n":15,"text":"एवं विदित्वा सर्वार्थानारभेदिति वैदिकम् ।\nनारभेदिति चान्यत्र नैष्ठिकी श्रूयते श्रुतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowing this, \"one should undertake all purposes\" is the Vedic word; \"one should not undertake\" is also heard elsewhere, in the final scripture."}},{"n":16,"text":"अनारम्भे ह्यदोषः स्यादारम्भेऽदोष उत्तमः ।\nएवं स्थितस्य शास्त्रस्य दुर्विज्ञेयं बलाबलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In not undertaking there is no fault, and in undertaking the best is without fault; so the relative strength of the scripture so placed is hard to know."}},{"n":17,"text":"यद्यत्र किंचित्प्रत्यक्षमहिंसायाः परं मतम् ।\nऋते त्वागमशास्त्रेभ्यो ब्रूहि तद्यदि पश्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"If here you see anything directly perceived that is higher than non-harm, other than the scriptures, then say it."}},{"text":"स्यूमरश्मिरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"Syumarashmi said:"}},{"n":18,"text":"स्वर्गकामो यजेतेति सततं श्रूयते श्रुतिः ।\nफलं प्रकल्प्य पूर्वं हि ततो यज्ञः प्रतायते ॥","meaning":{"en":"The scripture is constantly heard: \"One desiring heaven should sacrifice.\" Having first imagined the fruit, the sacrifice is then performed."}},{"n":19,"text":"अजश्चाश्वश्च मेषश्च गौश्च पक्षिगणाश्च ये ।\nग्राम्यारण्या ओषधयः प्राणस्यान्नमिति श्रुतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Goat, horse, sheep, cow, flocks of birds, and tame and wild herbs, the scripture says, are food for life."}},{"n":20,"text":"तथैवान्नं ह्यहरहः सायं प्रातर्निरुप्यते ।\nपशवश्चाथ धान्यं च यज्ञस्याङ्गमिति श्रुतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Likewise food is offered day by day, evening and morning; animals and grain are parts of the sacrifice, says the scripture."}},{"n":21,"text":"एतानि सह यज्ञेन प्रजापतिरकल्पयत् ।\nतेन प्रजापतिर्देवान्यज्ञेनायजत प्रभुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Prajapati arranged these along with the sacrifice; with that sacrifice the lord Prajapati worshipped the gods."}},{"n":22,"text":"ते स्मान्योन्यंचराः सर्वे प्राणिनः सप्त सप्त च ।\nयज्ञेषूपाकृतं विश्वं प्राहुरुत्तमसंज्ञितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"All creatures, tame and wild, seven and seven, move among each other; they say the universe is made ready in sacrifices, called the supreme."}},{"n":23,"text":"एतच्चैवाभ्यनुज्ञातं पूर्वैः पूर्वतरैस्तथा ।\nको जातु न विचिन्वीत विद्वान्स्वां शक्तिमात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This too was approved by those before and long before. What learned man would not examine his own capacity?"}},{"n":24,"text":"पशवश्च मनुष्याश्च द्रुमाश्चौषधिभिः सह ।\nस्वर्गमेवाभिकाङ्क्षन्ते न च स्वर्गस्त्वृते मखम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Animals, men, trees and plants all long for heaven alone, and there is no heaven without sacrifice."}},{"n":25,"text":"ओषध्यः पशवो वृक्षा वीरुदाज्यं पयो दधि ।\nहविर्भूमिर्दिशः श्रद्धा कालश्चैतानि द्वादश ॥","meaning":{"en":"Herbs, animals, trees, creepers, ghee, milk, curds, the oblation, earth, the directions, faith and time: these are twelve."}},{"n":26,"text":"ऋचो यजूंषि सामानि यजमानश्च षोडशः ।\nअग्निर्ज्ञेयो गृहपतिः स सप्तदश उच्यते ।\nअङ्गान्येतानि यज्ञस्य यज्ञो मूलमिति श्रुतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Rig, Yajur and Sama Vedas, and the sacrificer as the sixteenth. Fire, the lord of the house, is known as the seventeenth. These are the parts of sacrifice; the scripture says sacrifice is the root."}},{"n":27,"text":"आज्येन पयसा दध्ना शकृतामिक्षया त्वचा ।\nवालैः शृङ्गेण पादेन संभवत्येव गौर्मखम् ।\nएवं प्रत्येकशः सर्वं यद्यदस्य विधीयते ॥","meaning":{"en":"With ghee, milk, curds, dung, curd-cheese and hide, hair, horn and hoof, the cow becomes the sacrifice itself; so too each thing prescribed for it."}},{"n":28,"text":"यज्ञं वहन्ति संभूय सहर्त्विग्भिः सदक्षिणैः ।\nसंहत्यैतानि सर्वाणि यज्ञं निर्वर्तयन्त्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Together with the priests and the gifts they carry the sacrifice; all these combined accomplish it."}},{"n":29,"text":"यज्ञार्थानि हि सृष्टानि यथा वै श्रूयते श्रुतिः ।\nएवं पूर्वे पूर्वतराः प्रवृत्ताश्चैव मानवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"These were created for sacrifice, as the scripture is heard; so earlier and still earlier people acted."}},{"n":30,"text":"न हिनस्ति ह्यारभते नाभिद्रुह्यति किंचन ।\nयज्ञो यष्टव्य इत्येव यो यजत्यफलेप्सया ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who sacrifices without desire for fruit, thinking \"the sacrifice must be done,\" harms no one, begins nothing wrongly, and injures nothing."}},{"n":31,"text":"यज्ञाङ्गान्यपि चैतानि यथोक्तानि नसंशयः ।\nविधिना विधियुक्तानि तारयन्ति परस्परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"These parts of sacrifice, as stated, no doubt, when joined by rule, carry one another across."}},{"n":32,"text":"आम्नायमार्षं पश्यामि यस्मिन्वेदाः प्रतिष्ठिताः ।\nतं विद्वांसोऽनुपश्यन्ति ब्राह्मणस्यानुदर्शनात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I see the sage's tradition on which the Vedas rest; the learned see it by following the brahmin."}},{"n":33,"text":"ब्राह्मणप्रभवो यज्ञो ब्राह्मणार्पण एव च ।\nअनु यज्ञं जगत्सर्वं यज्ञश्चानु जगत्सदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sacrifice arises from the brahmin and is offered to the brahmin; the whole world follows sacrifice, and sacrifice follows the world."}},{"n":34,"text":"ओमिति ब्रह्मणो योनिर्नमः स्वाहा स्वधा वषट् ।\nयस्यैतानि प्रयुज्यन्ते यथाशक्ति कृतान्यपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Om is the womb of Brahman; so too namah, svaha, svadha, vashat. He by whom these are used, even as far as he can,"}},{"n":35,"text":"न तस्य त्रिषु लोकेषु परलोकभयं विदुः ।\nइति वेदा वदन्तीह सिद्धाश्च परमर्षयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"knows no fear of the next world in the three worlds. So the Vedas here say, and the perfected and great sages."}},{"n":36,"text":"ऋचो यजूंषि सामानि स्तोभाश्च विधिचोदिताः ।\nयस्मिन्नेतानि सर्वाणि बहिरेव स वै द्विजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Rik, Yajus and Saman verses and the chants, as the rule prescribes: he in whom all these remain only outside is the twice-born."}},{"n":37,"text":"अग्न्याधेये यद्भवति यच्च सोमे सुते द्विज ।\nयच्चेतरैर्महायज्ञैर्वेद तद्भगवान्स्वतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"What happens at the setting up of fires and at the Soma pressing, and what the other great sacrifices are, the Lord himself knows."}},{"n":38,"text":"तस्माद्ब्रह्मन्यजेतैव याजयेच्चाविचारयन् ।\nयजतः स्वर्गविधिना प्रेत्य स्वर्गफलं महत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, brahmin, one should sacrifice and have others sacrifice without hesitation. For one who sacrifices by the heavenly rule there is great reward in heaven after death."}},{"n":39,"text":"नायं लोकोऽस्त्ययज्ञानां परश्चेति विनिश्चयः ।\nवेदवादविदश्चैव प्रमाणमुभयं तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"It is settled that for those without sacrifice there is neither this world nor the next; and for the knowers of the Vedic word both are authority then."}}]}]}